# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#  Data Engineering Commit Message Template
#  Format: <type>(<scope>): <subject>
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#
# TYPE (choose one):
#   feat     – new feature or capability
#   fix      – bug fix
#   refactor – code restructure (no behaviour change)
#   perf     – performance improvement
#   docs     – documentation only
#   test     – add or update tests
#   chore    – build, deps, tooling changes
#   data     – data file or dataset changes
#   schema   – database/table schema changes
#   revert   – revert a previous commit
#
# SCOPE (choose one or combine):
#   data-ingestion   transformation   pipeline
#   quality          deployment       monitoring
#   infrastructure   dbt              airflow
#   glue             redshift         s3
#
# ── SUBJECT (line 1) ─────────────────────────────────────────
# • Use imperative mood: "add" not "added" / "adds"
# • Max 72 characters
# • No period at the end
#
# Examples:
#   feat(data-ingestion): add support for Parquet file format
#   fix(pipeline): handle null values in order_date column
#   perf(transformation): partition by date to reduce scan cost
#   schema(dbt): add customer_tier column to dim_customers
#   chore(deps): upgrade pandas to 2.1.0
#
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# <type>(<scope>): <subject — max 72 chars>


# ── BODY (optional — leave blank line above) ──────────────────
# Explain the WHY, not the what. What problem does this solve?
# Wrap at 72 characters.


# ── FOOTER (optional) ─────────────────────────────────────────
# Reference issues or tickets:
#   Closes #123
#   Refs #456
#   JIRA: DE-789
#   Breaking-Change: old API removed
#
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
